    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2TznfzA82m9ah28peK3HRxx)_\n\n## What\n- A heading titled `See also` (any case), with its subtree, is now a see-also section.\n- Every `id:` link in it is a mention of that concept, in list items or plain text.\n- Mentions have `:where` = `section` (weight 1.5, in `sp-see-also-where-weights`).\n\n## Scope\n- The scope is the parent of the section: the nearest ancestor with an `:ID:`.\n- At the bottom of the file (no ID'd ancestor) it belongs to the file.\n- An `:ID:` on the `See also` heading itself is ignored.\n- The open question above it counts, as for footnotes.\n\n## How\n- Reuses the footnote scanner: `sp-see-also-parse-buffer` gains an optional `SECTIONS` argument.\n- `sp-see-also-mentions-in-buffer` (cache and index) passes it, so `sp-see-also-show`, `sp-see-also-show-concept`, and the widgets and `concept-usage` block show them.\n- The sidenote renderer is unchanged: it calls the parser without `SECTIONS`.\n- Links already read as footnotes inside a section, and links in source/comment blocks, are not counted twice or at all.\n- Cache version 3, so files are re-read; editing a section re-reads only that file.\n- Literate source `sp-see-also.org` updated and re-tangled (new section \"See also\" sections, weights, tests).\n\n## Tests\n- 5 new ERT tests on fixtures; 25/25 pass in batch on Emacs 29.3.\n- **Not run on the real vault** or in a GUI/vulpea-ui.\n- Known limit: a heading in all capitals (`SEE ALSO`) is not matched (the existing title parser reads the first capital word as a keyword).\n- Branch is not number-prefixed: the number was unknown before creating the PR and the rename API is blocked.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAHAD2Bnx7dhWCdiE8)_",
